    <briefdescription>
<para>This structure contains the parameters of the derandomized encapsulation command, which exists for algorithm validation only (see XASU_MLKEM_ENCAPS_DERAND_CMD_ID). </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It carries the ordinary encapsulation parameters plus the message m to encapsulate with, laid out the same way <ref refid="struct_x_asu___key_manager_pqc_key_gen_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_KeyManagerPqcKeyGenParams</ref> appends a seed to the parameters it shares. The encapsulation key must be supplied through EncapsParams.KeyAddr: the key vault is not available to this command, so EncapsParams.KeyId must be zero. Unlike key generation, a zero SeedAddr is not a request to draw from the TRNG but an error, since supplying m is this command&apos;s only purpose. </para>    </detaileddescription>
